# A-2 under-reach override, cause freeze, and cause vocabulary — R-37 to R-39

Ruled 2026-09-23. Closes **Q-A** and **Q-B** from
`kyle-questions-2026-09-22-a2-override-and-cause-freeze.md`, which are A-2
brief **Appendix A** (override reason list) and **Appendix B** (when the cause
locks). Numbering continues from R-36.

**Provenance.** R-37: Kyle selected option C and directed the adverse-side
tenant limit be written in. R-38: Kyle selected option C. R-39: raised by Kyle
("make sure the cause reasons all make sense for a utility"); Claude's
recommendations accepted in full. Each ruling was issued in session against the
rule text re-fetched that day.

---

## 0. Verification basis

**Rule text re-fetched in full** from Cornell LII (16 Tex. Admin. Code §7.45,
provisions as amended effective 2004-07-12; LII's comparison tab reports no
prior version). The two clauses these rulings turn on were confirmed verbatim:

- (7)(B)(v)(I): the correction "may be foregone by the utility if the error is
  to the utility's disadvantage."
- (4)(E)(vi) closing clause: "unless the meter has been tampered with or unless
  such underbilling charges are due."

**The second discharges R-28's drafting caveat** that the closing clause was not
re-read on 2026-09-14. R-28's referral to counsel stands unchanged.

**Schema reach — limited.** `tu.sql` and the v5.4.2 patch series were not
reachable from this session. Method: `**/tu.sql`, `**/*v5_4_2*` and `**/*.sql`
globs across the only allowed root (`...\altteri`), plus a listing of
`/mnt/project`. **All schema cites below are against
`UBschema_current_5.13.2026.sql` and must be re-based against `tu.sql` before
entering a patch.** The AC-31 trigger shape (v5.4.2-10:332, column-listed
`BEFORE UPDATE OF billing_run_id, voided_invoice_id, rate_date_mode,
rate_date_override OR DELETE`) is carried from `a2-implementation-brief-2026-09-21.md`
§3 and was **not** independently verified.

### E-1 — Erratum to the 2026-09-22 record

R-34's operational scope note, F-3 and F-5 cite customer-requested tests and the
2.0% threshold at **§7.45(7)(A)(iv)**. No such paragraph exists: (7)(A) "Meter
requirements" has only clauses (i)–(iii). The correct cites are
**§7.45(7)(B)(iv)(I)** (customer-requested test, four-year look-back, fee) and
**§7.45(7)(B)(iv)(II)** (fee refund; 2.0% definition). The 2026-09-02 record
cites these correctly. **Substance of all three findings is unaffected.**

---

## R-37 — No override of the under-reach duty in the customer-favourable direction. Computed bounds, meter-scoped targeting and a date-validated hold replace it. Optional adverse-side tenant limit.

**Ruling.** Option C. The R-22/R-27 "override with a recorded reason" is
**withdrawn in the customer-favourable direction**. Four mechanisms take its
place; none of them forgoes a correction the rule makes mandatory.

**(a) Computed bound — the defective meter's service, not an operator reason.**

```
window_start = MAX(anchor − 6 months,
                   governing prior test date (R-34),
                   start of the defective meter's deployments within the window)
```

Readings at this location taken by a *different* meter are not "previous
readings" of the defective meter and were never in scope. The bound is computed
from `meter_deployments` (snapshot 3356–3377: `meter_id`, `location_id`,
`install_date NOT NULL`, `removal_date`, `removal_reason`) and written to the
R-25 evidence row. No operator input.

*Distinct from R-35 refinement 3, and must not be conflated with it:* a
deployment start date may **bound** the window, because earlier readings are not
readings of this meter. It may **never** be treated **as a test date**.

**(b) Target the meter's readings, not the account's invoices.** Every in-window
reading of the defective meter is in scope, **across every deployment and every
occupant**. Two consequences:

- *Customer turnover inside the window* is not under-reach. Periods billed to a
  customer whose service has ended are delivered to that customer as a
  **monetary adjustment**, per (v)(I) ("unless service is terminated, in which
  event a monetary adjustment is to be made"). A former customer who cannot be
  located is handed to the tenant's unclaimed-property process — not forgone,
**K-04.** Neutral internal terms ("sales service" and "transportation service") with a per-jurisdiction label table, and the tenant supplies the exact tariff wording at setup. The pipeline safety fee is an effective-dated rule with amount, basis (per customer or per service line), billing timing, citation and optional recovery-report deadline. Research notes for Texas: a 2009 law raised the per-service-line cap to one dollar, but the current Utilities Code §121.211 text limits total fees to program cost and the Commission sets the amount by rule (16 TAC §8.201), so there is no single fixed cap. One 2024 tariff shows $1.22 per customer, and another requires a recovery report within 90 days after the last billing cycle in which the fee is billed. Confirm the current amount against §8.201 before loading it.

## Wave 7 decisions

**R-11.** Estimation, late fees and program exclusions all become dated rule data with a legal citation.

**K-06.**
- No early-pay discounts, because gas is regulated. Drop that rule type.
- The meter test fee is outcome-driven, with tolerance and fee as rule data, confirmed with the tenant at setup.
- Rounding goes to the cent, and rates and intermediate math carry four decimals (0.0000). Kyle confirmed 2026-10-15: standard rounding to the nearest cent, which can go either up or down (half-up at the midpoint).
- Accessible notice formats: a customer preference field (large print, braille, language) and a record of the format actually sent.

**K-07.** Support municipal utilities with rules entered per utility and no assumed defaults. Not required at launch.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.stamp_log_created_at() RETURNS trigger
    LANGUAGE plpgsql
    SET search_path = public, pg_temp
    AS $$
BEGIN
    IF NOT (SELECT r.rolsuper FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles r WHERE r.rolname = current_user) OR NEW.created_at IS NULL THEN
        NEW.created_at := now();
    END IF;
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;
COMMENT ON FUNCTION public.stamp_log_created_at() IS
    'v5.4.2-19. BEFORE INSERT on an append-only log: created_at is stamped with the transaction time; a superuser''s value is kept (history loads).';

